      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture of the original test. I'll improve understandability by:\n- Removing unused constants (`TESTKEY2`) and imports (`HashMap`, `Map`)\n- Removing commented-out debug code\n- Renaming the opaque `check()` method to something descriptive\n- Adding meaningful assertion messages to aid diagnosis on failure\n- Giving `assertLookupNotEmpty` a slightly more descriptive structureThe improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed unused `TESTKEY2` constant and unused `HashMap`/`Map` imports, deleted the commented-out debug `println`, renamed the opaque `check()` method to `assertAllDefaultLookupsWork()` to self-document its intent, and added descriptive failure messages to assertions so test failures pinpoint which lookup broke."
    }
